    {
      "id": "A2.F7",
      "text": "VGGT Depth Anything 3 DUSt3R MipNeRF Figure 7 : Probing internal representations for fundamental matrix approximation. We successfully recover the fundamental matrix from all three models, also on the MipNeRF360 dataset, but with higher error values. However, the emergence trends remain the same as for other datasets.",
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "id": "A2.F8",
      "text": "VGGT Depth Anything 3 DUSt3R Synthetic Real data Figure 8 : Probing internal representations for fundamental matrix approximation. We successfully recover the fundamental matrix from all three models on both synthetic and real-world datasets when using a linear probe. We report the same trends as for the MLP probe, but with higher errors.",
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "id": "A2.F9",
      "text": "VGGT Depth Anything 3 DUSt3R Synthetic Real data Figure 9 : Probing internal representations for fundamental matrix approximation. We successfully recover the fundamental matrix from all three models on both synthetic and real-world datasets with an MLP probe trained only for 1 epoch. We report the same trends, but the error values are significantly higher.",
      "images": []
    },
    {
      "id": "A2.F10",
      "text": "VGGT Depth Anything 3 DUSt3R Synthetic Figure 10 : Rank ratio. Ratio of smallest and largest singular values across layers on different data splits for the probing experiment from fig. 1 . A good fundamental matrix should have a significant difference between the largest and smallest singular values.",
      "images": []
    },
